  "body": "A vertical 2-axis cut of the bottom flower of a lofted opening (walls run from (10.34,0,0) to (7.5,0,20)) enters the part by about 1.3 mm at Z10 and 2.8 mm near the top. Verify says \"358 move(s) gouge; the deepest reading at any height is 0.1620 mm\" - the kerf offset, not the depth - and the slug law reports only at Z2.501. The post is still blocked (safe), but the reported size is wrong.\n\nDone means: the gouge reading reports the real deepest entry over the part height (test on a lofted wall where the depth is known analytically).\n\nFound in a wire EDM validation run of CamCraft 0.24.0 through the camcraft MCP (2026-11-21), on test parts in `~/Desktop/camcraft/edm-validation/` (EDM-T1 square, EDM-T2 2-axis block, EDM-T3 taper block) and a Sodick owner's own UV part (#617). Wire EDM-W025 (0.25 mm), Sodick ALC400G with test conditions.",
